4 true] [17592186251569 1145 "We're told that $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=7.$ According to the definition of continuity, this means that ${lim}_{x\\to 7}f(x)$ exists and\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {7}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to 7}f(x)=f(7)=13.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {7}^{-}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}-f(x)) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({7}^{2}-13) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(36) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({6}^{2}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251571 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251572 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251573 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251574 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251575 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1041 "selection" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251571 13194139533794 true] [17592186251570 1110 #uuid "17786bf9-1ca1-59ee-9cea-4709fc3100b3" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251571 1034 "2\\operatorname{ln}⁡6" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251571 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533794 true] [17592186251571 1111 #uuid "71b699f2-7405-5059-a7ec-7b5c5c37942f" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251572 1034 "6\\sqrt{2}" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251572 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533794 true] [17592186251572 1111 #uuid "1360e0fe-8eaa-57c6-8106-b5133b25fd0d" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251573 1034 "\\operatorname{ln}⁡6" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251573 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533794 true] [17592186251573 1111 #uuid "29cab8b8-72ad-5d84-a326-05c28d62cf90" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251574 1034 "36" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251574 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533794 true] [17592186251574 1111 #uuid "3d3e13c8-f7e8-5392-a6c2-96992bb41259" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251575 1034 "6" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251575 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139533794 true] [17592186251575 1111 #uuid "9f021756-67d6-5e55-9b02-c6128655c431" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251576 1017 #edb/ref 17592186251577 13194139533794 true] [17592186251576 1089 "q-152913" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251576 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533794 true] [17592186251576 1100 "Consider the following function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}x+1, & x<0 \\\\ 0, & x=0 \\\\ {e}^{-x}, & x>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding $f(x)?$\n\n- $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0$\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)$ exists\n- ${lim}_{x\\to \\,0}f(x)=f(0)$\n- $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=0$" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251576 1113 #uuid "86e8b7b9-d7d8-5f9b-a33a-a4700cd37236" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251576 1145 "To test for continuity of $f(x)$ at a point $x=c$, we need to check three conditions:\n\n- Does $f(c)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)$ exist?\n\n- Does ${lim}_{x\\to c}f(x)=f(c)?$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true. Using the expression for the middle branch of the function, we obtain that \n\n$$\nf(0)=0.\n$$\n\nSo, $f(x)$ is defined at $x=0.$ $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement II is true. By calculating the one-sided limits, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}(x+1) \\\\  & =(0)+1 \\\\  & =1 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}({e}^{-x}) \\\\  & ={e}^{0} \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=0$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=1\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 0}f(x)=1\\ne f(0).$  $\\,\\,\\times $\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since not all statements I-III are true, the function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" 13194139533794 true] [1