\  & =-4-2 \\\\  & =-6 \\\\ {lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x) & ={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}(-3x) \\\\  & =-3(2) \\\\  & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAs a result:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to {2}^{-}}f(x)={lim}_{x\\to {2}^{+}}f(x)\n$$\n\n \nTherefore, the limit of $f(x)$ at $x=2$ exists:\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-6\\,\\,✓\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, we have that ${lim}_{x\\to 2}f(x)=-6=f(2).$  $\\,\\,✓$\n\n- Statement IV is false. Since all statements I-III are true, according to the continuity test, the function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III only.\"" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251599 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251600 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251601 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251602 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1000 #edb/ref 17592186251603 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1041 "selection" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1104 #edb/ref 17592186251602 13194139533794 true] [17592186251598 1110 #uuid "ee64c490-5138-5fc7-9f6b-9c529d9ee604" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251599 1034 "None of the statements are true" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251599 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533794 true] [17592186251599 1111 #uuid "865f9605-d157-562c-a78e-7e32f332ca7e" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251600 1034 "I only" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251600 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533794 true] [17592186251600 1111 #uuid "235dbeb3-10ba-5180-b565-3def804f73e3" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251601 1034 "I and II only" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251601 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533794 true] [17592186251601 1111 #uuid "1ee093d1-d3c3-5215-8ebb-784938c84622" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251602 1034 "I, II, and III only" 13194139533794 true] [17592186251602 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139533794 true] [17